            "status": "fixed",
            "status_notes": "Fixed by composer.json conflict phpoffice/phpspreadsheet <1.30.7. Advisory names CVE-2024-45048 (GHSA-ghg6-32f9-2jp7, XXE), fixed in phpoffice/phpspreadsheet 1.29.1; the 2.x target in the advisory is not installable with pimcore/pimcore 10.6.9 (^1.15). The floor 1.30.7 is the first 1.x release without a published 1.x advisory, so it also covers the 28 advisories fixed after 1.29.1 and the two fixed in 1.29.1 itself (CVE-2024-45293, CVE-2024-45046). Run composer update phpoffice/phpspreadsheet once."
        },
        {
            "vulnerability": {
                "name": "GHSA-jmh9-6rjq-gjh9"
            },
            "products": [
                {
                    "@id": "pkg:composer/pimcore/pimcore@10.6.9",
                    "identifiers": {
                        "purl": "pkg:composer/pimcore/pimcore@10.6.9"
                    }
                },
                {
                    "@id": "pkg:composer/pimcore/pimcore@v10.6.9",
                    "identifiers": {
                        "purl": "pkg:composer/pimcore/pimcore@v10.6.9"
                    }
                }
            ],
            "status": "fixed",
            "status_notes": "Fixed by patches/pimcore-GHSA-jmh9-6rjq-gjh9-minipaint-jquery.patch, patches/pimcore-GHSA-jmh9-6rjq-gjh9-minipaint-csp.patch. jQuery 3.4.1 is a private webpack module of the image editor (bundle.js module 42, no window.$). CVE-2020-11022: jQuery.htmlPrefilter becomes an identity function. CVE-2020-11023 (option wrapped in select) does not reproduce in Chrome 157, Firefox 159 or jsdom and is not changed in jQuery. Both are closed at page level: the image editor response carries a Content-Security-Policy without 'unsafe-inline' and 'unsafe-eval' in script-src, one nonce for the inline config script and sha256 hashes for the 22 fixed inline handler strings of the minipaint dialogs, so an onerror or other handler created by HTML parsing never runs. Untrusted data does reach jQuery HTML parsing (Image > Information puts EXIF values and file name of a file opened via File > Open into a div.trn that the translate plugin re-parses): a 38 character EXIF value and an option/select payload with an inline onerror execute on the unpatched editor in Chrome 157 and Firefox 159 and are inert with the policy, with and without the jQuery patch. The full menu (94 entries) and all 21 tools open without a policy violation. Run bin/console assets:install and bin/console cache:clear after applying; bundle.js.map is not regenerated."
        },
